title: TextAnimatorShowcase
---
Walter: Suuure you are...[waitfor=0.3][/waitfor]that's the mid-line pause, waitfor.

Owen: Alright, let's test every effect Text Animator's got. #save_checkpoint

Owen: [shake]This one's the classic — shake.[/shake]

Isla: [wiggle]And this is wiggle, a little looser than shake.[/wiggle]

Walter: [wave]Wave rolls up and down, letter by letter.[/wave]

Player: [bounce]Bounce hops each letter up and back down.[/bounce]

Owen: [swing]Swing rocks side to side, like a pendulum.[/swing]

Isla: [pend]This is the actual pendulum effect, pend.[/pend]

Walter: [dangle]Dangle lets letters droop and sway loosely.[/dangle]

Player: [rot]Rotate spins each letter slightly, called rot.[/rot]

Owen: [slideh]Slide moves letters in from the side — slideh.[/slideh]

Isla: [incr]Increase Size makes letters grow, tagged incr, not size.[/incr]

Walter: [rainb]Rainbow cycles color across the text.[/rainb]

Player: [fade]Fade eases letters in and out of visibility.[/fade]

Owen: You can stack effects too, like [shake][rainb]this shaking rainbow[/rainb][/shake].

Isla: Amplitude and speed are tunable — try [shake a=5]a strong shake[/shake] or [wave s=3]a fast wave[/wave].



Owen: That's the full built-in set. Mix, match, and stack away. #save_checkpoint
===
